      "worked_solution": "Since $△TUV$ is an isosceles triangle with base $\\overset{―}{TV}$, we have that $\\overset{―}{TU}≅\\overset{―}{UV}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TU & =UV \\\\ 5x-8 & =4x+3 \\\\ x & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe perimeter of $△TUV$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =TU+UV+TV \\\\  & =(5x-8)+(4x+3)+(2x+5) \\\\  & =11x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $x=11$ in the expression for the perimeter, we get\n\n$$\np=11x=11(11)=121.\n$$\n\nHence, $p=121.$",
